.Dd June 28, 2026
.Dt FIBMGR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fibmgr
.Nd A simple management tool for FreeBSD's FIB (Forwarding Information Base)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 4 \&| Fl 6
.Cm copy
.Ar source_fib
.Cm to
.Ar target_fib
.Op Ar target_fib ...
.No \&| Cm all
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl 4 \&| Fl 6
.Cm clear
.Ar target_fib
.Op Ar target_fib ...
.No \&| Cm all
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a lightweight command-line utility designed to simplify the management of FIBs (Forwarding Information Bases / routing tables) in
.Fx
systems.
It enables system administrators to quickly copy routing rules from a specific source FIB to multiple target FIBs, or bulk-clear routing data from specified FIBs.
.Pp
The tool offers flexible argument passing, allowing multiple target FIBs to be specified using either comma-separated or space-separated formats, as well as supporting the special
.Cm all
keyword for global operations.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following global options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl 4
Apply operations to IPv4 routing tables only.
.It Fl 6
Apply operations to IPv6 routing tables only.
.El
.Pp
If not specified, both IPv4 and IPv6 routing tables are processed.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm copy
Copies routing information from a source FIB
.Pq Ar source_fib
to one or more target FIBs
.Pq Ar target_fib .
.Pp
.Sy Syntax :
.Cm copy
.Ar source_fib
.Cm to
.Ar target_fib1 Ns Oo , Ns Ar target_fib2 ... Oc
.Pp
.Sy The Cm all Sy Argument :
When the target FIB is specified as
.Cm all ,
the utility copies the source routing table to all available FIBs in the system.
.It Cm clear
Clears routing information from one or more target FIBs
.Pq Ar target_fib .
.Pp
.Sy Syntax :
.Cm clear
.Ar target_fib1 Ns Oo , Ns Ar target_fib2 ... Oc
.Pp
.Sy The Cm all Sy Argument :
When the target FIB is specified as
.Cm all ,
the utility clears all FIBs in the system (use with caution).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Below are some common use cases and configuration examples:
.Pp
.Sy 1. Copying FIB Data
.Pp
Copy routing table from FIB 0 to FIB 1 and FIB 2 (comma-separated):
.Dl fibmgr copy 0 to 1,2
.Pp
Copy routing table from FIB 0 to FIB 1, 2, and 3 (space-separated):
.Dl fibmgr copy 0 to 1 2 3
.Pp
Mix comma and space separators for multiple target FIBs:
.Dl fibmgr copy 0 to 1,2 3
.Pp
Copy the routing table from FIB 0 to all available FIBs:
.Dl fibmgr copy 0 to all
.Pp
Copy only the IPv4 routing table from FIB 0 to all FIBs:
.Dl fibmgr -4 copy 0 to all
.Pp
.Sy 2. Clearing FIB Data
.Pp
Clear the routing tables of FIB 1 and FIB 2:
.Dl fibmgr clear 1,2
.Pp
Clear the routing tables of FIB 1, 2, and 3 (space-separated):
.Dl fibmgr clear 1 2 3
.Pp
Clear specified multiple FIBs using mixed formatting:
.Dl fibmgr clear 1,2 3
.Pp
Clear all FIBs in the system:
.Dl fibmgr clear all
.Pp
Clear only the IPv6 routing data across all FIBs:
.Dl fibmgr -6 clear all
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
Compiling the source code of this project requires
.Fx
14.2 or higher.
The source code will fail to compile successfully on any system versions prior to 14.2.